Changes to the source of the speech synthesis engine

The speaking libraries of this plugin are built from audio.cpp,
Copyright 2026 ShugoAI LLC, at revision
3174e6b26f11a0e39b4f150961dce98f43ba860d, under the Apache License, Version
2.0, which is this repository's licence too (LICENSE, at its root). The builds
do not take that revision's source as it stands. The five files in this
directory stand in place of the engine's own files of the same path, and two
more of the engine's files are replaced by the two files in
../windows_resident/overrides, which the notice there states.

Together the five files, and two places of mimi_decoder.cpp there, make the
transformer blocks of the Pocket speech model compute GELU by its tanh
approximation, as that model's reference implementation does
(pocket_tts/modules/transformer.py: F.gelu(..., approximate="tanh")), where
the engine's transformer blocks compute it by erf. Blocks of the engine's
other models keep the engine's default.

Each file in this directory is listed here with where it comes from and what
was changed.

vec.h
  Upstream: external/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/vec.h
  Upstream sha256: 9b55ac2d0c79bf7d9dba1a0efe8c8ef9a40a3775c0086841a2d3eb93388ac96c
  As built sha256: 81a3ed7c862e4c828a5857814776e449b2da5a564c7b23aec836b8038f8aeb1e
  Changed: four lines added and one removed, in one place. GGML_GELU_FP16 is
  defined only where GGML_GELU_FORCE_F32 is not. A build that defines
  GGML_GELU_FORCE_F32, as this plugin's builds of the speaking library do,
  then computes GELU on 32-bit floats and not through ggml's 16-bit table.
  Nothing else differs.
  This file is ggml's, which the engine carries under external/ggml. ggml is
  distributed under the MIT License reproduced at the end of this notice, and
  the modified copy stays under that licence.

transformer_blocks.h
  Upstream: include/engine/framework/modules/attention/transformer_blocks.h
  Upstream sha256: e3bde0b338e726f92985624084ef532d27e82594a005164c90a832ffb75df12a
  As built sha256: c303faef82cd5bc0bc5fe216c86e40eaf070683f6eb3102976556462eaf2d862
  Changed: one line added. TransformerEncoderBlockConfig gains the member
  gelu_approximation, GeluApproximation::ExactErf where nothing sets it.
  Nothing else differs.

transformer_blocks.cpp
  Upstream: src/framework/modules/attention/transformer_blocks.cpp
  Upstream sha256: ba6c4ec5af6affa3b3f396937d4ce73f002a309c0a3affc065c602708ca2056e
  As built sha256: 68edfc940d9bce261d5f4c57cb601131f65fb627180978a46ed318ad8a610b07
  Changed: two lines, in two places. The feed-forward module that
  TransformerEncoderBlockModule::build and
  StreamingTransformerEncoderBlockModule::build make is given the
  configuration's gelu_approximation, where upstream gives it
  GeluApproximation::ExactErf. Nothing else differs.

flow_lm.cpp
  Upstream: src/models/pocket_tts/flow_lm.cpp
  Upstream sha256: 7f60cad2e4a3364c594e94e2ff597f928c40cac7d890b864418f508a90016297
  As built sha256: 40f55d48971f72fce61be995af4432cc35a201c7c5b2fdc3e15fd726da6a7080
  Changed: three lines added and four removed, in one place. The streaming
  transformer block of the flow model is configured through
  graph_common::pocket_transformer_config, with the hidden size, the heads,
  the intermediate size and the epsilon upstream writes there. Nothing else
  differs.

graph_common.h
  Upstream: src/models/pocket_tts/graph_common.h
  Upstream sha256: a16717241c8e8e6e18a1ec37aa44c6213a53c140794ebe324e6a2d31de4a40c5
  As built sha256: 5ebdf6cb7c80e33d389ae5cca5d870afb996a5d524ee88ff24b66fbaee16b9f8
  Changed: ten lines added in one place, the function
  pocket_transformer_config. It returns the block configuration upstream
  writes where it is used (those four values, no bias) with
  gelu_approximation set to GeluApproximation::Tanh. Nothing else differs.

"As built" is the file that stood in the engine source the Windows and the
macOS libraries were built from, which is the file here without its four-line
head comment; a test holds the two to that. "Upstream" is the file of the
upstream repository at the revision above.

WHAT WAS COMPARED. The engine source the Windows libraries were built from and
the one the macOS libraries were built from were each compared with the
upstream revision file by file: 4,524 files, none missing and none added.
Each differs from upstream in the five files here and in mimi_decoder.cpp; the
macOS one also in acoustic_model.cpp and in the bundled ggml's Metal backend
(../metal-library-beside.patch), which that build applies in the source, where
the Windows build compiles its two replaced files from their own directory. A
script of the engine's Windows build that no library is compiled from differs
by its line ends alone. Nothing else differs. The Windows build also compiles
three files that scripts/stage_native_path_shim.py derives from the engine's
own.

The Linux library is stated apart, in ../engine_overrides_linux/NOTICE: how
it was built is not recorded, an engine source of that time is kept, and it
differs from upstream in the five files here, in three more, and in the three
files scripts/stage_native_path_shim.py derives.

